# Renders are NOT committed — the repo keeps the recipe, not the film
# (design 025 §8a, and the same rule the sibling demos follow). Rebuild with
# ./make-demo.sh <demo>; the .srt files ARE kept, because they are text, they are
# what gets attached to a YouTube upload as the caption track, and they are the
# only artefact here a reviewer can read in a diff.
out/**/*.mp4

# scratch
.build/
.smoke/
*.log

# _bin/rysh is a symlink to an absolute path on the machine that recorded, so it
# cannot be committed usefully. make-demo.sh recreates it if it is missing.
_bin/
